WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.235
[birds chirping]

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:19.819
You are Mari the housekeeper.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.686
He's told me of you.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.171
[thud]

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:13.473
Some creatures must go
back to go wild, it seems.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.276
Monsieur Trepagny smashes
them with his stick at night

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:19.045
and they know to stay
away from our bed.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.280
He does have
dominion over all.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.917
As his wife, I will therefore
need you to serve my needs.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.788
Help me see to the house so
that I may improve the estate

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.824
and have it well on
the way to prospering

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:36.463
so that our children may in turn
enjoy the bounty of this land.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.198
You will bear no children.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.966
MELISSANDE: I am the
lady of the house.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.801
I steer the man.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:45.505
In time, I will steer
him any way I want.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:50.677
To renovate, toss out old habits
back into the forest where

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.478
they belong.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.217
There is my dear husband.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.168
CLAUDE: I was out
searching for Sel

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:16.803
and I found something, Mari.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:27.446
These seem to have run
away from my sanctum.

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:30.416
What do you know about this?

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.652
Nothing.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.754
And Monsieur Sel?

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.457
He took has departed.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:42.328
I go away for one day and
my doma falls to disorder.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.863
You saw nothing at all?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.299
As the housekeeper, you
should be aware of the comings

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.101
and goings on the estate.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.469
A dog could do better.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.770
[smash]

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:56.643
Perhaps you can discover what
has happened to Monsieur Sel.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.811
I will speak alone
with Melissande.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.513
[tense music]

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.285
Go on.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.591
[door slamming]

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:17.063
I see now the arrangement who
wish to design for yourself.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.198
I have made no such
designs, my cherie.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.935
I wish to do only beautiful
things in this doma

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:27.140
and you will be my partner
in this, and as my partner,

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:30.310
you will learn to look
past my many flaws,

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.813
and I will look past
your shortcomings,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.815
which I'm sure are few.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.150
[exhales]

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.087
Did you know that I
sailed across an ocean

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.356
and walked into
the endless forest

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:45.291
that I could find
the correct man

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.294
to bestow my maiden head on?

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.828
That is no small thing.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:54.500
There are deeper bindings
towards which we must work.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.569
The binding of the
two into a one.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:59.739
There will be no more
binding nor any more bedding

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.976
until you tell me the truth.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.844
I gave it once.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.879
I may never give it again.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.448
Which truth this?

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.883
There are so many
floating about.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.619
Pluck one for me
and I will tell it.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.821
Mari.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:15.989
Yes.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:16.756
MELISSANDE: You
have lain with her.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.327
What would you have me do?

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:24.297
You have given her a son.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.864
Did she tell you that?

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.166
MELISSANDE: Nobody
told me a thing.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:31.471
I have eyes-- a brain.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:35.875
They will know when you've
gone to visit her cabin

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.411
and when you have not.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:42.815
We will have a proper
wedding ceremony.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.350
I will wear a special dress.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.551
There will be dancing.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.219
Yes, of course.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:50.056
We will have a
wonderful ceremony.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:55.628
Now I am brimming with ideas
on how to improve the doma.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:59.666
You spoke true of its
beauty, but it must be tamed.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:03.436
Not everything will lay
down for you, Melissande.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.538
This is my doma.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:10.209
And as its master, I must stride
it with vigor and authority.

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:13.146
You may stride anywhere
you like with as much vigor

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.747
as you may muster.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:20.086
But your visit Mari's
cabin at your own peril.

